# React's TYPES have to be visible to third-party packages, not just to ours.
#
# pnpm's default layout gives each dependency only what it declares. Packages
# that ship .d.ts files referencing `react` — recharts, input-otp, and most of
# the component libraries here — do not depend on @types/react, because it is a
# devDependency concern for whoever compiles them. So when TypeScript reads
# their declarations it resolves `react` to the untyped JS package and silently
# degrades: SVGProps<T> contributes nothing, Context<T> collapses to {}.
#
# The symptom is never "types are missing". It is a specific, confusing error in
# OUR code about a property that plainly exists:
#
#   input-otp  →  Property 'slots' does not exist on type '{}'
#   recharts   →  Property 'fill' does not exist on type '… ReferenceAreaProps'
#
# Both were real, both survived review, and both looked like our bug. Hoisting
# the React types to the root node_modules puts them where TypeScript's upward
# lookup finds them from inside any package.
public-hoist-pattern[]=@types/react
public-hoist-pattern[]=@types/react-dom
